-- title:
--   Joint real analyticity of the Gaussian kernel
-- statement:
--   For every dimension $d\ge0$, the function $$ (x,\theta)\mapsto\varphi_d(x-\theta)=(2\pi)^{-d/2}e^{-\|x-\theta\|^2/2} $$ is real analytic at every point of $\mathbb R^d\times\mathbb R^d$. Joint analyticity permits the incidence argument to differentiate simultaneously in locations and observations.
